Sentence 1: Trump family
Trump family Trump (; ; ) is a German and German-American family, descended from Johann Philipp Trump (1667–1707) from Kallstadt, then in the Electoral Palatinate, Holy Roman Empire, today in modern Germany.
Sentence 2: While the surname Trump is found throughout Germany, it is recorded as the name of this family in Kallstadt since the 17th century, where many family members were winegrowers.
Sentence 3: Family members also still live in the family's ancestral region in southwestern Germany.
Sentence 4: They are part of the broader Trump family originating from Germany.
Sentence 5: The original Trump family in Germany are Lutheran members of the Evangelical Church of the Palatinate, although that region has been overwhelmingly Calvinist since Frederick III, Elector Palatine introduced the Reformed faith in the mid 16th century.
