Worms, Germany Worms () is a city in Rhineland-Palatinate, Germany, situated on the Upper Rhine about south-southwest of Frankfurt-am-Main.
Sentence 2: A pre-Roman foundation, Worms was the capital of the Kingdom of the Burgundians in the early 5th century and hence the scene of the medieval legends referring to this period, notably the first part of the "Nibelungenlied".
Sentence 3: Worms has been a Roman Catholic bishopric since at least 614, and was an important palatinate of Charlemagne.
Sentence 4: Worms Cathedral is one of the Imperial Cathedrals and among the finest examples of Romanesque architecture in Germany.
