Sentence 2: Formerly a military installation known as Dow Air Force Base, Bangor International Airport remains home to the 101st Air Refueling Wing of the Maine Air National Guard, although most of the Air Force's aircraft and personnel left in the late 1960s.
Sentence 3: Bangor International Airport was the main ground setting for Stephen King's novella "The Langoliers", which was made into a two-part television miniseries.
