Sentence 2: Similarly, Ushaw College of Durham University hosted until 2011 a Roman Catholic seminary that had been established in 1568 in Douai in northern France and which relocated to Ushaw Moor, four miles west of Durham in 1808 but did not become part of the University (as a Licensed Hall) until 1968.
Sentence 3: Durham University already has a much stronger claim to be the third-oldest university through its creation by Act of Parliament in 1832.
