Sentence 1: Rhythm section
Rhythm section A rhythm section (also called a backup band) is a group of musicians within a music ensemble or band who provide the underlying rhythm, harmony and pulse of the accompaniment, providing a rhythmic and harmonic reference and "beat" for the rest of the band.
Sentence 2: Many of the rhythm section instruments, such as keyboard instruments and guitars, are used to play the chord progression upon which the song is based.
