Sentence 4: Brake pad
Brake pad Brake pads are a component of disc brakes used in automotive and other applications.
Sentence 5: Brake pads are steel backing plates with friction material bound to the surface that faces the disc brake rotor.
Sentence 6: In disc brakes, there are usually two brake pads per disc rotor.
Sentence 7: Unlike a drum brake, the disc brake has no self-servo effect—the braking force is always proportional to the pressure applied on the braking pedal lever.
Sentence 8: However many disc brake systems have servo assistance ("Brake Booster") to reduce the driver's pedal effort.
