Sentence 2: Yavuz Selim Mosque
Yavuz Selim Mosque The Yavuz Selim Mosque, also known as the Selim I Mosque and the Yavuz Sultan Selim Mosque () is a 16th-century Ottoman imperial mosque located at the top of the 5th Hill of Istanbul, Turkey, in the neighborhood of Çukurbostan, overlooking the Golden Horn.
Sentence 3: Its size and geographic position make it a familiar landmark on the Istanbul skyline.
Sentence 4: The Yavuz Selim Mosque is the second oldest extant imperial mosque in Istanbul.
