Sentence 1: Unix
Unix Unix (; trademarked as UNIX) is a family of multitasking, multiuser computer operating systems that derive from the original AT&T Unix, development starting in the 1970s at the Bell Labs research center by Ken Thompson, Dennis Ritchie, and others.
Sentence 2: Bell Labs produced several versions of Unix that are collectively referred to as "Research Unix".
