Sentence 1: Hyacinthoides
Hyacinthoides Hyacinthoides is a genus of flowering plants in the family Asparagaceae, known as bluebells.
Sentence 2: "Hyacinthoides" is classified in the subfamily Scilloideae (now part of the family Asparagaceae, but formerly treated as a separate family, called Hyacinthaceae), alongside genera such as "Scilla", "Chionodoxa" and "Ornithogalum".
Sentence 3: "Hyacinthoides" is differentiated from these other genera by the presence of two bracts at the base of each flower, rather than one bract per flower or no bracts in the other genera.
Sentence 4: They are known commonly as cat's eyes and popcorn flowers (the latter name is also used to refer to the closely related genus "Plagiobothrys").
