Sentence 1: Mount Vernon Ladies' Association
Mount Vernon Ladies' Association The Mount Vernon Ladies' Association is a non-profit organization that preserves and maintains the Mount Vernon estate originally owned by George Washington and family.
Sentence 2: After the deaths of George Washington (in 1799) and his widow Martha (in 1802), Mount Vernon remained in the family for three generations.
Sentence 3: John Augustine Washington III, a great-great-nephew of George Washington, eventually inherited the property, but he could not afford to maintain it.
Sentence 4: Following Martha Washington's death in 1802, George Washington's will was carried out in accordance with the terms of his bequests.
Sentence 5: Notes Citations Mount Vernon Mount Vernon was the plantation of George Washington, the first President of the United States, and his wife, Martha Dandridge Custis Washington.
