Sentence 1: Ruminococcus
Ruminococcus Ruminococcus is a genus of bacteria in the class Clostridia.
Sentence 2: As usual, bacteria taxonomy is in flux, with Clostridia being paraphyletic, and some erroneous members of "Ruminococcus" being reassigned to a new genus "Blautia" on the basis of 16S rRNA gene sequences.
