Sentence 1: Pickens, South Carolina
Pickens, South Carolina Pickens, formerly called Pickens Courthouse, is a city in Pickens County, South Carolina, United States.
Sentence 2: Pickens changed its classification from a town to a city in 1998, but it was not reported to the Census Bureau until 2001.
Sentence 3: It is the county seat of Pickens County.
Sentence 4: It was named after Andrew Pickens (1739–1817), an American revolutionary soldier and US Congressman for South Carolina.
