Sentence 1: Game of the Goose
Game of the Goose The Game of the Goose or Goose game is a board game where two or more players move pieces around a track by rolling a dice.
Sentence 2: The aim of the game is to reach square number sixty-three before any of the other players, while avoiding obstacles such as the Inn, the Bridge and Death.
Sentence 3: The game is thought to have originated in the 16th century, and is considered the prototype of many of the commercial European racing board games of later centuries.
Sentence 4: The game is mostly played in Europe and seen as family entertainment.
