Sentence 3: Gymnosperm
Gymnosperm The gymnosperms , also known as Acrogymnospermae, are a group of seed-producing plants that includes conifers, cycads, "Ginkgo", and gnetophytes.
Sentence 4: The term "gymnosperm" comes from the Greek composite word "γυμνόσπερμος" (γυμνός gymnos, "naked" and σπέρμα sperma, "seed"), meaning "naked seeds".
Sentence 5: The non-encased condition of their seeds stands in contrast to the seeds and ovules of flowering plants (angiosperms), which are enclosed within an ovary.
Sentence 6: Gymnosperm seeds develop either on the surface of scales or leaves, which are often modified to form cones,
Sentence 7: The family is also known as the sundew family.
