Sentence 2: It typically refers to anti-tank variants of existing tank chassis with a well-armoured casemate fixed superstructure, mounting an anti-tank gun with limited traverse in the front, and usually classed by the western Allies of World War II as a tank destroyer.
Sentence 3: Jagdtiger
Jagdtiger Jagdtiger ("Hunting Tiger") is the common name of a German turretless heavy tank destroyer of World War II.
Sentence 4: The 71-tonne "Jagdtiger" was the heaviest armored fighting vehicle used operationally during World War II and is the heaviest armored vehicle of any type to achieve series production.
Sentence 5: Panzerfaust The Panzerfaust (, "armor fist" or "tank fist", plural: "Panzerfäuste") is an inexpensive, single shot, recoilless German anti-tank weapon of World War II.
