Sentence 1: American Bulldog
American Bulldog The American Bulldog is a breed of utility dog descended from the Old English Bulldog.
Sentence 2: The Old English Bulldog was preserved by working class immigrants who brought their working dogs with them to the American South.
Sentence 3: Small farmers and ranchers used this all-around working dog for many tasks including farm guardians, stock dogs and catch dogs.
Sentence 4: These dogs were not an actual breed as considered by today's standards but were a generic bulldog type.
Sentence 5: There were no recorded pedigrees or records and breeding decisions were dependent on the best working farm dogs despite breed or background.
