Sentence 2: They are counted as one of the 56 ethnic groups officially recognized by the People's Republic of China.
Sentence 3: The Sui are descended from the ancient Baiyue peoples, who had inhabited southern China before the Han dynasty (Wei 2003:viii).
Sentence 4: Today, 93% of all Sui people (322,000 individuals) reside in Guizhou, China, with about half of them living in Sandu Shui Autonomous County.
