Sentence 1: Himalchuli
Himalchuli Himalchuli is the second highest mountain in the Mansiri Himal, part of the Nepalese Himalayas.
Sentence 2: Himalchuli has three main peaks: East (7893 m), West (7540 m) and North (7371 m).
Sentence 3: Himalchuli is the 18th highest mountain in the world (using a cutoff of 500m prominence, or re-ascent).
Sentence 4: Himalchuli is also notable for its large vertical relief over local terrain.
