Sentence 2: Bryophyte
Bryophyte Bryophytes are an informal group consisting of three divisions of non-vascular land plants (embryophytes): the liverworts, hornworts and mosses.
Sentence 3: Bryophytes produce enclosed reproductive structures (gametangia and sporangia), but they do not produce flowers or seeds.
Sentence 4: Bryophytes are usually considered to be a paraphyletic group and not a monophyletic group, although some studies have produced contrary results.
