Sentence 1: Jurisdictional Immunities of the State
Jurisdictional Immunities of the State Jurisdictional Immunities of the State (Germany v. Italy: Greece Intervening) was a case concerning the extent of state immunity before the International Court of Justice.
Sentence 2: The court found that Italy was wrong to ignore German immunity, and found that Italy was obligated to render the decisions of its courts against Germany without effect.
