Sentence 3: Alcohol law
U.S. states limit alcohol sales in grocery stores and gas stations to beer at or below 3.2% alcohol: Colorado, Kansas, Minnesota, Oklahoma, and Utah.
Sentence 4: In Oklahoma, liquor stores may not refrigerate any beverage containing more than 3.2% alcohol.
Sentence 5: Alcohol laws of Kansas
Alcohol laws of Kansas The alcohol laws of Kansas are among the strictest in the United States, in sharp contrast to its neighboring state of Missouri (see Alcohol laws of Missouri), and similar to (though somewhat less rigid than) its other neighboring state of Oklahoma (see Alcohol laws of Oklahoma).
