Sentence 1: Tomb of the Unknown Confederate Soldier
Tomb of the Unknown Confederate Soldier The Tomb of the Unknown Confederate Soldier is a tomb on the grounds of Beauvoir in Biloxi, Harrison County, Mississippi, that holds the remains of an unidentified Confederate soldier of the American Civil War.
Sentence 2: The remains were discovered in late 1979 by Ben Akselson of Beaumont, Texas, member of the Sons of Confederate Veterans, and Rick Forte, Chairman of the Combined Boards of Beauvoir, on a battlefield of the Vicksburg Campaign.
Sentence 3: The discovery led to the establishment of the Tomb of the Unknown Confederate Soldier in the Confederate Veterans Cemetery at Beauvoir.
Sentence 4: The medal awarded to the Unknown Soldier was on display in the Beauvoir Confederate Museum.
