Sentence 1: La Comédie humaine
La Comédie humaine La Comédie humaine (, "The Human Comedy") is the title of Honoré de Balzac's (1799–1850) multi-volume collection of interlinked novels and stories depicting French society in the period of the Restoration (1815–1830) and the July Monarchy (1830–1848).
Sentence 2: Honorine (novel) Honorine is an 1843 novel by French novelist and playwright Honoré de Balzac (1799-1850) and included in his series of novels (or "Roman-fleuve") known as "La Comédie humaine" ("The Human Comedy") which parodies and depicts French society in the period of the Restoration and the July Monarchy (1815-1848).
Sentence 3: He was also the author of a biography of Honoré de Balzac, and a comprehensive study of Balzac's writings: "Balzac's 'Comédie Humaine"' (1959).
