Sentence 1: Liverpool Metropolitan Cathedral
Liverpool Metropolitan Cathedral Liverpool Metropolitan Cathedral, officially known as the Metropolitan Cathedral of Christ the King, is the seat of the Archbishop of Liverpool and the mother church of the Roman Catholic Archdiocese of Liverpool in Liverpool, England.
Sentence 2: Liverpool's wealth as a port city enabled the construction of two enormous cathedrals, both dating from the 20th century.
Sentence 3: The Roman Catholic Metropolitan Cathedral of Liverpool is situated approximately half a mile to the north.
Sentence 4: The cathedrals are linked by Hope Street, which takes its name from William Hope, a local merchant whose house stood on the site now occupied by the Philharmonic Hall, and was named long before either cathedral was built.
