Sentence 1: Rorqual
Rorqual Rorquals (Balaenopteridae) are the largest group of baleen whales, a family with nine extant species in two genera.
Sentence 2: They include what is believed to be the largest animal that has ever lived, the blue whale, which can reach , and the fin whale, which reaches ; even the smallest of the group, the northern minke whale, reaches .
Sentence 3: Rorquals take their name from French ', which derives from the Norwegian word ', meaning "rorqual-whale" (the first element "røyr" originated from the Old Norse name for this type of whale, "reyðr", probably related to the Norse word for "red").
