Sentence 3: Geography of Colombia
Geography of Colombia The Republic of Colombia is a transcontinental country largely situated in the northwest of South America, with territories in North America.
Sentence 4: Colombia is the 26th largest nation in the world and the fourth-largest country in South America after Brazil, Argentina, and Peru.
Sentence 5: Colombia is the only South American country which borders both the Atlantic and Pacific Oceans.
Sentence 6: The country is located where three lithospheric plates—Nazca, Caribbean, and South American—converge, and their movement produces different types of geologic faults.
Sentence 7: It is the fourth largest South American country and only country in South America to have coasts in the Pacific and Caribbean ocean.
