Sentence 1: Cumberland Mountain is roughly parallel to Pine Mountain which lies from eight to ten miles to the northwest.
Sentence 2: The northwestern slope of Pine Mountain is cliff-lined (escarpment slope) whereas the southeastern slope is gentle, this is the dip slope and it is roughly parallel to the dip of the sandstones.
Sentence 3: Several gaps occur along Pine Mountain and these are usually caused by erosion along cross-cutting faults.
Sentence 4: The gap was formed by the development of three major structural features: the Pine Mountain Thrust Sheet, the Middlesboro Syncline, and the Rocky Face Fault.
Sentence 5: Resistance on the fault from the opposing Cumberland Mountain to Pine Mountain caused the U-shaped structure of the Middlesboro Syncline. 81%|████████  | 18311/22607 [13:49:47<4:35:21,  3.85s/it][transformers] Both `max_new_tokens` (=256) and `max_length`(=4096) seem to have been set. `max_new_tokens` will take precedence. Please refer to the documentation for more information. (https://huggingface.co/docs/transformers/main/en/main_classes/text_generation)
