Sentence 2: An existential study of ordinary lives led by two alienated urban white collar workers, "Accidental Life" was the only feature film of Ante Peterlić, Croatian film theorist and film critic.
Sentence 3: The film received mediocre reviews and went largely unnoticed after its release, but has been reevaluated decades later as one of the best Croatian films ever made.
