Sentence 1: Buzzword bingo
Buzzword bingo Buzzword bingo, also known as bullshit bingo, is a bingo-style game where participants prepare bingo cards with buzzwords and tick them off when they are uttered during an event, such as a meeting or speech.
Sentence 2: The goal of the game is to tick off a predetermined number of words in a row and then signal bingo to other players.
Sentence 3: Buzzword bingo is generally played in situations where audience members feel that the speaker is relying too heavily on buzzwords or jargon rather than providing relevant details or clarity.
Sentence 4: Buzzword bingo
the word "Bingo" within the context of a comment or question.
Sentence 5: Other versions of the game require actually yelling "Bingo!"
Sentence 6: To avoid the reprimands that would likely result from doing so, participants may resort to looking at one another and silently mouthing the word "Bingo" instead.
Sentence 7: An example of a buzzword bingo card for a business management meeting is shown below.
